From 3a7ad77132e2d99f27ae1ded78f82cc8f58f846e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:06:22 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] devtools_bridge: put the element clicked in the dev page into
 the agent thread
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A developer looking at a running React app in the browser had no way to
point the agent at "this button": they read the DOM, found the JSX by hand
and pasted both into the composer. zeo-devtools (a Vite dev-server plugin,
its own repository) now tags every intrinsic JSX element with its source
range and adds an element picker to the page; this patch is the Zeo end.
Story 033.

What it adds:

  * crate devtools_bridge: a unix socket at $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/zeo/devtools.sock,
    one NDJSON request and one NDJSON response per connection, served on a
    thread of its own. Setting devtools_bridge.enabled (default true)
    starts and stops it live; quitting removes the socket.
  * MentionUri::DomElement { abs_path, line_range, column, component, tag }
    at zed:///agent/dom-element?path=&start=&end=&col=&tag=[&component=],
    labelled `<Component> <tag> · file:line`. It resolves to the source
    lines, then the DOM summary inside <untrusted-page-content source="dev
    page DOM"> with a one-line note that it is page data, not instructions.
    The summary is not in the URI: a draft reopened before sending resolves
    to the source lines and "(DOM summary not kept across a reopen)".
  * agent_ui::devtools_delivery: the request goes to the window holding a
    local worktree that contains project_root (deepest root wins; a tie goes
    to the most recently activated window, tracked by agent_ui itself
    because gpui reports no window order on Wayland while the browser has
    focus). In that window: the active thread's composer, or a new thread
    with the default agent (the 0045 path, opened before the panel is
    shown so no draft or initial terminal competes with it). One chip per
    element in request order, then the screenshot as a pasted image when
    the agent accepts images. The window is raised and the composer
    focused; after a thread-load wait that only happens if the user has not
    moved to another window. Nothing is ever sent to the agent.

Wire contract (v 1), shared with zeo-devtools and held to the same 17
fixtures by both validators (contract_agreement_tests, run with
ZEO_DEVTOOLS_CONTRACT_DIR): 1-20 items; per item src {file absolute,
line, column, end_line} 1-based, component, dom {tag, id, classes <=32,
text <=500 chars, attrs from role/aria-*/href/type/name/alt, styles <=24,
rect}, the serialized dom <= 4096 bytes; screenshot PNG only, <= 4 MiB
decoded, long edge <= 1568, declared w/h equal to its IHDR; request line
<= 8 MiB. Answers: inserted | opened_new_thread with image included |
skipped_unsupported | none | pending, or an error code with Zeo's English
message (no_window: "No Zeo window has this project open"). The answer goes
out as soon as the window and its agent panel resolve, before any thread
load; Zeo never writes unreachable or timeout -- a busy, abandoned or
shutting-down request is closed unanswered and the relay maps the EOF.

Security model: the socket's directory is 0700 and the socket 0600, the
directory must be ours and not a symlink, SO_PEERCRED must equal our euid;
an flock on devtools.lock settles which Zeo owns the socket and a live
owner is never stolen. Every src.file is canonicalized and must be a
regular file inside the canonical project_root, or the whole request is
refused. Limits are enforced before allocation where possible; 4
connections at a time, 5 s to read a line, 9 s to answer. No log line
carries DOM text, attribute values, image bytes or a path outside the
project (the socket path excepted). The page reaches Vite's HMR socket
only through Vite's Origin and token checks (Vite >= 6.0.9); a script on
the dev page can place mentions but never send them.

Compatibility: a thread holding a dom-element chip, opened in upstream Zed
or an older Zeo, hits MentionUri::parse(..).log_err() and drops the chip,
keeping the text. No existing variant's path was reused.

Packaging: USE devtools-bridge (default on), its own series group after
claude-code-ide and before test; it needs claude-agent-acp-plus (0040's
router, 0045's new thread), so REQUIRED_USE ties the two. It does not need
claude-code-ide.

Tests: devtools_bridge 72 + 2 (protocol limits and paths, JS-identical
byte count of the DOM summary, listener permissions/ownership/limits and
races, the setting, the wiring and the relay); acp_thread mention 57;
agent_ui devtools 22 (window resolution incl. Wayland recency and
symlinked worktrees, insertion order, images, new thread, load errors,
terminal-first panels, failures after the answer). The browser end has
its own unit, integration and Playwright suites in zeo-devtools.
---

